Subject: [PATCH 14/15] feat: add brainstorm, onboard, refactor-plan skills;
 require examples.md for every skill; rebrand display name to Vivantel KMS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three new skills fill gaps this plugin didn't cover: brainstorm
generates and synthesizes unanchored approaches to a problem before
any decision exists (deliberately never reads the knowledge base);
onboard turns the knowledge base into a role-tailored ramp-up plan
instead of leaving a new contributor to reconstruct it manually;
refactor-plan produces a phased, guardrail-respecting plan for a
bounded change, flagging any step that would violate a guardrail for
confirmation instead of silently dropping or working around it. All
three are read-only/write-nothing, matching this plugin's existing
planning-skill discipline.

Every skill now ships a colocated examples.md (2-3 worked usage
examples), retrofitted onto all 8 pre-existing skills too so the
plugin doesn't ship half-documented — enforced going forward by a new
lint check rather than left to manual review.

Separately, the plugin's display name changes from "KMS Dev Skills" to
"Vivantel KMS", expanded on first mention as "Vivantel KMS (Knowledge
Management System)" everywhere it's introduced to a user or
contributor — "KMS" alone read as an unexplained acronym. Technical
identifiers (name: "kms", the /plugin install kms slug, the
plugins/kms/ directory) are unchanged, to avoid a breaking change for
existing installs.

Both plugin manifests bumped 0.2.1 -> 0.3.0 together, per the
manifest-version-sync guardrail.

